From 47fcd13684ece686870c9f6635661b82c7e822af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:23:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] fix(engine): fail a membership in a set of functions over
 a set TLC overrides as TLC does

TLC tests f \in [D -> R] by comparing f's domain with D
(SetOfFcnsValue.member). Where D is a set it overrides, Nat, Int,
STRING or Seq(S), that comparison fails (UserValue.equals): "Attempted
to check equality of the set {1} with the value:\nNat", or "Attempted
to compare overridden value STRING with non-overridden value". The
engine enumerated D to compare it and stopped at its own limit, so the
run declined. It now fails as TLC does, which the trace evaluator words
as TLC words it.

Runs that declined so now match TLC (startup fixtures
function-set-member-*). The next commit makes a union's membership test
reach this test where TLC's does, which without this declines a run
that matched before.
